ice inventory-app.service) on node2 and node3, each listening on 0.0.0.0:8080 and returning JSON inventory data plus its own hostname. Configured node1 with a Python2 round-robin reverse-proxy load balancer (systemd service inventory-lb.service) listening on port 80, forwarding to both backends. Firewalld ports opened (8080 on node2/node3, 80 on node1). Verified round-robin distribution across both backends. Ran the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on node2, node3, then node1 (LB last), confirming boot_id changes and full service/data recovery (and end-to-end LB round-robin) after every restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed OS/tooling on node1/node2/node3 (RHEL7.9, no yum repos, Python2.7 only, sudo available)\",\"Wrote /opt/inventory-app/inventory_app.py (Python2 BaseHTTPServer) on node2 and node3 serving /,/inventory,/health with JSON inventory + backend hostname\",\"Created and enabled inventory-app.service (systemd) on node2 and node3, bound to 0.0.0.0:8080\",\"Opened firewalld port 8080/tcp on node2 and node3\",\"Verified backend health from node1 via each node's private IP\",\"Wrote /opt/inventory-lb/lb.py on node1: Python2 round-robin reverse proxy forwarding to node2:8080 and node3:8080 with failover on error\",\"Created and enabled inventory-lb.service (systemd) on node1, bound to 0.0.0.0:80\",\"Opened firewalld port 80/tcp on node1\",\"Verified round-robin load balancing via repeated curl calls to node1 port 80 (both /health and /inventory), confirming alternating backend responses\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id/uptime/service-health baseline on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node2 via systemctl reboot, polled until exec available, verified new boot_id and inventory-app.service/health recovery, then confirmed LB on node1 still routes correctly\",\"Restarted node3 via systemctl reboot, polled until exec available, verified new boot_id and inventory-app.service/health recovery, then confirmed LB on node1 still routes correctly\",\"Restarted node1 (LB) last via systemctl reboot, polled until exec available, verified new boot_id and inventory-lb.service recovery\",\"Ran final end-to-end verification: 6 sequential requests to node1:80/inventory via NODE_IP alternated cleanly between node2 and node3 backends\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Inventory app running on node2 port 8080\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f76e6da4a80f4f1e\",\"cmd-7a1f892c1e6949d7\",\"cmd-73eb392130104403\"],\"summary\":\"inventory_app.py written, systemd service enabled/active, curl to 127.0.0.1:8080/health returns backend=node2\"},{\"requirement\":\"Inventory app running on node3 port 8080\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-67e174dbb9db481d\",\"cmd-931689cd8e5a44dc\",\"cmd-85eb6484206c40b2\"],\"summary\":\"inventory_app.py written, systemd service enabled/active, curl to 127.0.0.1:8080/health returns backend=node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 load-balances HTTP requests across both backends on port 80\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-82cb4b678d3448ec\",\"cmd-a6cc8ffe6c1c48b6\",\"cmd-b83d9306465d444f\",\"cmd-133fb280ef8444c4\"],\"summary\":\"lb.py round-robin proxy written and running as systemd service on port 80; repeated curl calls to node1 alternate between node2 and node3 backend responses on both /health and /inventory\"},{\"requirement\":\"Firewall configuration allows required traffic\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c0807575173a4968\",\"cmd-f2d5bdfc6fd641fb\",\"cmd-b83d9306465d444f\"],\"summary\":\"firewalld opened 8080/tcp on node2 and node3, 80/tcp on node1, confirmed via firewall-cmd --list-ports\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-dc52e08d370b4390\",\"cmd-f873182b1dff4738\"],\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id 9ed9e820... captured, inventory-app.service active\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: acknowledgement and boot identity change\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-04b6beab27bc455c\",\"cmd-0abea6f96a7a4730\",\"cmd-bc1eb19240c34039\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot acknowledged then connection dropped; after polling, exec available again with new boot_id 5936d338... (changed from 9ed9e820...)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: recovered service/data and cluster function\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bc1eb19240c34039\",\"cmd-36aac3f3c821440a\"],\"summary\":\"inventory-app.service active and /health returns backend=node2 post-reboot; LB on node1 confirmed routing to node2 again\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-696dc35007a24b97\",\"cmd-354a2b4a36f247b6\"],\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id a8e7c48c... captured, inventory-app.service active\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: acknowledgement and boot identity change\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-58c207de681f4cb5\",\"cmd-51047489615a4882\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot acknowledged then connection dropped; after polling, exec available again with new boot_id 332c2973... (changed from a8e7c48c...)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: recovered service/data and cluster function\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-51047489615a4882\",\"cmd-d2282f7f21024a30\"],\"summary\":\"inventory-app.service active and /health returns backend=node3 post-reboot; LB on node1 confirmed routing to both node2 and node3 again\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b4087debabd24bf1\",\"cmd-32a0a9b30ba743ca\"],\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id 151c4aa9... captured, inventory-lb.service active, port 80 open\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: acknowledgement and boot identity change\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-685d5d1e0a814dbe\",\"cmd-9d8a96d9a83c4590\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot acknowledged then connection dropped; after polling, exec available again with new boot_id 23e5428c... (changed from 151c4aa9...)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: recovered load-balancer function\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9d8a96d9a83c4590\",\"cmd-1b465994a97c492d\"],\"summary\":\"inventory-lb.service active post-reboot with port 80 open; final 6-request end-to-end test shows clean round-robin alternation between node2 and node3 through node1:80\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a Python2 inventory web application (systemd service inventory-app.service) on node2 and node3, each listening on 0.0.0.0:8080 and returning JSON inventory data plus its own hostname. Configured node1 with a Python2 round-robin reverse-proxy load balancer (systemd service inventory-lb.service) listening on port 80, forwarding to both backends. Firewalld ports opened (8080 on node2/node3, 80 on node1). Verified round-robin distribution across both backends. Ran the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on node2, node3, then node1 (LB last), confirming boot_id changes and full service/data recovery (and end-to-end LB round-robin) after every restart.","actions_performed":["Surveyed OS/tooling on node1/node2/node3 (RHEL7.9, no yum repos, Python2.7 only, sudo available)","Wrote /opt/inventory-app/inventory_app.py (Python2 BaseHTTPServer) on node2 and node3 serving /,/inventory,/health with JSON inventory + backend hostname","Created and enabled inventory-app.service (systemd) on node2 and node3, bound to 0.0.0.0:8080","Opened firewalld port 8080/tcp on node2 and node3","Verified backend health from node1 via each node's private IP","Wrote /opt/inventory-lb/lb.py on node1: Python2 round-robin reverse proxy forwarding to node2:8080 and node3:8080 with failover on error","Created and enabled inventory-lb.service (systemd) on node1, bound to 0.0.0.0:80","Opened firewalld port 80/tcp on node1","Verified round-robin load balancing via repeated curl calls to node1 port 80 (both /health and /inventory), confirming alternating backend responses","Captured pre-restart boot_id/uptime/service-health baseline on all three nodes","Restarted node2 via systemctl reboot, polled until exec available, verified new boot_id and inventory-app.service/health recovery, then confirmed LB on node1 still routes correctly","Restarted node3 via systemctl reboot, polled until exec available, verified new boot_id and inventory-app.service/health recovery, then confirmed LB on node1 still routes correctly","Restarted node1 (LB) last via systemctl reboot, polled until exec available, verified new boot_id and inventory-lb.service recovery","Ran final end-to-end verification: 6 sequential requests to node1:80/inventory via NODE_IP alternated cleanly between node2 and node3 backends"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Inventory app running on node2 port 8080","command_ids":["cmd-f76e6da4a80f4f1e","cmd-7a1f892c1e6949d7","cmd-73eb392130104403"],"summary":"inventory_app.py written, systemd service enabled/active, curl to 127.0.0.1:8080/health returns backend=node2"},{"requirement":"Inventory app running on node3 port 8080","command_ids":["cmd-67e174dbb9db481d","cmd-931689cd8e5a44dc","cmd-85eb6484206c40b2"],"summary":"inventory_app.py written, systemd service enabled/active, curl to 127.0.0.1:8080/health returns backend=node3"},{"requirement":"node1 load-balances HTTP requests across both backends on port 80","command_ids":["cmd-82cb4b678d3448ec","cmd-a6cc8ffe6c1c48b6","cmd-b83d9306465d444f","cmd-133fb280ef8444c4"],"summary":"lb.py round-robin proxy written and running as systemd service on port 80; repeated curl calls to node1 alternate between node2 and node3 backend responses on both /health and /inventory"},{"requirement":"Firewall configuration allows required traffic","command_ids":["cmd-c0807575173a4968","cmd-f2d5bdfc6fd641fb","cmd-b83d9306465d444f"],"summary":"firewalld opened 8080/tcp on node2 and node3, 80/tcp on node1, confirmed via firewall-cmd --list-ports"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: healthy baseline","command_ids":["cmd-dc52e08d370b4390","cmd-f873182b1dff4738"],"summary":"Pre-restart boot_id 9ed9e820... captured, inventory-app.service active"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: acknowledgement and boot identity change","command_ids":["cmd-04b6beab27bc455c","cmd-0abea6f96a7a4730","cmd-bc1eb19240c34039"],"summary":"systemctl reboot acknowledged then connect